17	+Plan custody now uses the same SQLite family and filesystem-alias collision
18	+rules as archive outputs. `retain_plan` takes the verified source, rejects its
19	+main/sidecar names before creating a file, and still retains private exact bytes.
20	+`read_plan_for_copy` checks both source and destination families before the CLI
21	+opens either database. The bare `read_plan` function is only a bounded decoder;
22	+it confers no path-safety guarantee. These checks retain the trusted-filesystem
23	+assumption; they do not fence hostile concurrent filesystem replacement.
